## 1. Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  Panel["AtmospherePanel (Dashboard tab)"] -->|set| Store["useAtmosphere (zustand + persist)"]
  Store -->|subscribe: colors/params| Uniforms["atmosphereUniforms (singleton)"]
  Ctrl["AtmosphereController (single useFrame)"] -->|uTime, uCamPos, uGlowDir| Uniforms
  Ctrl -->|FogExp2 + background| Scene["scene.fog / scene.background"]
  Uniforms --> Sky["SkyDome ShaderMaterial"]
  Uniforms --> Grass["Grass / Trees / Flowers"]
  Uniforms --> Simon["SimonGlow shader"]
  Uniforms --> Patched["GLB MeshStandardMaterials (onBeforeCompile)"]
  Uniforms --> Pillars["Hero + depth-layer pillars"]
  Store --> Lights["AtmosphereLighting"]
  Store --> Post["AtmospherePostFX"]
```

Key rules:
- **One store** ([lib/atmosphere.ts](file:///d:/CODE/Particles/src/lib/atmosphere.ts)) holds only serializable data (hex strings, numbers, tuples). It is persisted to `localStorage`.
- **One uniform object**, `atmosphereUniforms`. Every material spreads it into its own uniforms (`{ ...own, ...atmosphereUniforms }`). Spreading copies *references* to the same `{ value }` objects, so one write updates every material.
  > Never `UniformsUtils.clone()` the shared part. SimonGlowSystem currently clones, so it will merge the shared uniforms *after* cloning.
- **Fog color is derived**: `fogColor = lerp(horizon, zenith, 0.15)` in linear space, unless `decoupleFog` is on.
- **Sky and fog share one GLSL function**, `atmosphereInscatter(dir)`. At `dir.y = 0` the sky returns exactly this value, and fully fogged geometry returns the same value. So the seam is mathematically impossible, not just tuned away.

