## 4. Depth layers: `src/components/atmosphere/DepthLayers.tsx`

Config-driven list: hero (about 40u from the hero-shot camera), mid (about 120u), far (about 260u), plus an optional 4th even further out. The hero top's world position is written to the store, where it drives `uGlowDir` (tracked mode) and the rim light target.

Expected fog factor `f` with the defaults (density 0.012, falloff 0.04). These come from the TS mirror:

| Layer | Dist | f at base (y=0) | f at y=15 | Read |
|-------|------|-----------------|-----------|------|
| Hero | 40 | 0.27 | 0.19 | crisp, high contrast |
| Mid | 120 | 0.83 | 0.59 | dark soft silhouette |
| Far | 260 | 0.998 | 0.71 | barely-visible shape |
| Ground | 400 | ≈1.000 | — | equals the horizon/fog color |

Height fog makes bases dissolve faster than tops, which is exactly what the far pillar in the reference does.

