## 10. Tunables: what they do and good ranges

| Param | Default | Range | What it does |
|-------|---------|-------|--------------|
| Horizon Color | `#b3000a` | dark–mid crimson | Main haze hue; fog is derived from it |
| Zenith Color | `#3a0004` | very dark red | Top of sky and vignette tint; fog leans 15% toward it |
| Glow Color | `#ff1a1a` | saturated red | Backlight lobe in the sky and on fogged silhouettes; rim light |
| Glow Strength | 0.55 | 0.2–1.0 | Lobe brightness; >1 starts to clip |
| Fog Density | 0.012 | 0.006–0.025 | Distance where layers separate; 0 = off, 0.05 = wall |
| Fog Height Falloff | 0.04 | 0.01–0.1 | Higher = fog hugs the ground, tops stay visible |
| Fog Height Base | 0 | ground Y ± 10 | Altitude where height fog is densest |
| Sky Exposure | 1.0 | 0.5–1.5 | Trim only, no more 3.9× hack |
| Cloud Scale | 1.4 | 0.6–3.0 | Smaller = bigger, softer smoke blobs |
| Cloud Speed | 0.015 | 0–0.05 | Drift; forced to 0 on low quality |
| Cloud Contrast | 1.3 | 0.5–2.5 | Mottling strength |
| Ambient | 0.25 | 0.15–0.35 | Shadow-side fill; higher flattens depth |
| Rim Intensity | 4.0 | 2–8 | Backlight on the hero's edges and top |
| Rim White Mix | 0.45 | 0–1 | 0 = pure glowColor rim (strict spec), ~0.5 = near-white top like the reference |
| Bloom | 0.6 | 0.3–1.0 | Threshold 0.6, so only the hot top edge blooms |
| Vignette | 0.75 | 0.5–0.9 | Darkens edges and bottom toward zenith |
| Grain | 0.12 | 0.06–0.18 | Visible but subtle above ~0.1 |

